{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem remembered Sarah.</b> Everywhere it says וה׳‎, it means He and His court. He sat in judgment upon her, as it is written 'if she has not been defiled etc.' — and she was pure and cleared of suspicion, and also bore seed and gave birth to a male; and Sarah was secluded and was not defiled. And one should not raise a difficulty from 'וה׳‎ Shaddai made heaven,' for its meaning is thus: He is the merciful one together with the attribute of judgment — 'made heaven.' As I explained regarding 'on the day that HaShem Elohim made earth and heaven.'" "<b>Et Sarah.</b> To include all barren women." "<b>As He said.</b> 'I will return' — 'I will return.'" "<b>As He spoke.</b> On that day HaShem cut a covenant with Abraham etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:08.401240693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}